#basePath P3_Pheromones
#include "Header.leaf"

:: Start
@exposed
@trigger    OnLocationChanged
// "NONE" ensures no other threads are in-progress
// global:currentPhase == 3 ensures player is in phase 3
@when       global:currentThread == "NONE", global:currentPhase == 3, location == "ResearchLab"
@cutscene
// Lock all location on map
$call SetInThreadLocks()
$call DisableMapButton()

// Mark start of thread
$set global:currentThread = "P3_Pheromones"

{@}   
       You can hear Arjan's... less-than-intact... phonograph through the door to the research lab.
       The door swings open before you knock. 

{@Arjan}
       Haha. Told you I was psychic. 
       I'm not. Come in. 

{@}
       You follow him inside. 
       He's looking over into large vats. When you peek over his shoulder, you see they're filled with sea lamprey.

{@Arjan}
       I imagine you're not just here to admire my clothes.

{@You}
       Oh, haha, no. I came to ask you questions about your research. 
       Someone at the Army Corps told me it could be useful in making traps more effective?

{@Arjan}
       Oh, yes, my research. I'm looking into pheromones. 

{@You}
       Which are...?

{@Arjan}
       Pheromones are scents that some animals produce to communicate with others.
       In this case, I'm looking at two particular pheromes that sea lamprey utilize.
       One which is a warning of danger, and another which is to signal to a potential mate.
       The idea is one will repel sea lamprey and the other will attract them.

{@You}
       So you could use it to attract or repel sea lamprey to the traps that have been placed in tributaries.

{@Arjan}
       Potentially making them more effective. 
       That's the goal, anyway. 
$call GiveEvidenceChip("Evidence-Pheromones")

{@You}
       That seems like a great idea.

{@Arjan}
       I like to think so, too.
       But you'll have to get permission from the townsfolk to be able to use it. 
       People are rightfully skeptical about putting chemicals into the water.
       If you already have a lot of contacts, that could be easy, but if not, you'll have to go to another town hall meeting.

{@You}
       Thanks for the heads up. 
       Oh, and before I go, I have something for you. 

{@Arjan}
       Is that so?

{@}
       You fish a small music box from your bag.

{@You}
       I know it's not quite as antique as the other things you collect, but I figure you'd like it. 
       I used to use it a lot as a kid, but I haven't in a while, and I figure you'd take better care of it. 

{@Arjan}
       Thank you, Ana. I'll cherish it.

{@}
       You watch him put it next to the phonograph, a warm feeling in your belly. 

$call UnlockLocation(TownHall)
// IF high Community/Communicate stat, optional skip townsfolk wary section
$if StatCheck(Communicate, 3)
       $call UnlockLocation(DNROffice) // Place Pheromones
$endif
$call EnableMapButton()


:: AtTownHall
@trigger    OnLocationChanged
// global:currentThread ensures the correct thread
// global:currentPhase == 3 ensures player is in phase 3
@when       global:currentThread == "P3_Pheromones", global:currentPhase == 3, location == "TownHall"
// Lock all location on map
$call SetInThreadLocks()
$call DisableMapButton()

{@}   
       The town hall meeting is in full swing when you walk in. 
       You find a moment to bring your question up to the group. 

{@You}
       Hello everyone. It's me, Ana, with Sea Grant again. 
       We're looking into a new program in conjunction with the university.
       We would use pheromones, or scents that sea lamprey are sensitive to, to make traps more effective.

{@Fisher}
       Is this more chemicals in the water?

{@You}
       Yes, these are a kind of chemical. 
       But they are a naturally occuring type of chemical, just like the pheromones that the sea lamprey naturally make.

{@Fisher}
       But isn't it different when it's manmade.

{@You}
       It's the same structure. 
       Just like if I said we'd made H2O in a lab, it would be the same water that you can buy in the store.
       It's true that people are exposed to harmful chemicals sometimes. We have to be vigilant about that.
       But the goal of scientists working for public health isn't to poison you. They do a lot of research to make sure things are safe.
       I understand if you are hesitant. I understand that indigenous communities might not want chemical intervention. 
       And if that's the consensus that the town decides on, me and all the scientists will accept it.
       All we ask is that you give it a chance.

{@}
       There are murmurs through the crowd. 
       At the front, the mayor raises her hand. 

{@Mayor}
       Thank you for bringing this to our attention. 
       The city council is prepared to allow it with careful checks to ensure the longterm safety. 
       This will only take place in municipal waters, of course.

{@}
       The crowd murmurs an assenting sound. 

{@You}
       Thank you. And thank you, everyone. 

{@}
       On your way out, you see Paul smile and nod at you. Proud.

// TODO: Rest of Town Hall section here

// TODO: Give evidence chip
$call GiveEvidenceChip("Evidence-wary-townfolk")

$call UnlockLocation(DNROffice) // Place Pheromones
$call EnableMapButton()



:: AtDNROffice
@trigger    OnLocationChanged
// global:currentThread ensures the correct thread
// global:currentPhase == 3 ensures player is in phase 3
@when       global:currentThread == "P3_Pheromones", global:currentPhase == 3, location == "DNROffice"
// Lock all location on map
$call SetInThreadLocks()
$call DisableMapButton()

{@}   
       Paul is once again at his desk.

{@You}
       How's the set going?

{@Paul}
       Mm. I'm downloading the files now. I'd say I'm ready. 
       And I'd say you are, too.

{@You}
       You think so?

{@Paul}
       Mm. You have the agreement of the town.
       I'll begin the process of organizing with Arjan to get the pheromones ready to place in the tributaries. 
       Whenever you need it, just let me know. I'll be here. 
$call GiveActionCard("Action-pheromones")

{@You}
       Thanks, Paul. I mean it. 

$if !HasSeen(P3_UpstreamBarriers.End) //ensures final dialogue with Paul doesn't happen twice
       //does nothing in case player has already seen the dialogue
$else
{@You}
       There's one more thing. In the end, you were right.

{@Paul}
       Hmm?

{@You}
       Earlier, you asked me about what I thought about coming to town. 
       I didn't like how much it'd changed. 
       But the future is a gift. I'm glad I'm here to see it. 

{@Paul}
       There's no time like the present. 

{@}
       You can't help but agree. 
$endif
// TODO: Rest of DNR Office section here

$call UnlockLocation(DNROffice) // Place Pheromones
$call EnableMapButton()

// skip to end
$goto .End


:: End
@exposed
@tracked

// Mark end of thread
$set global:currentThread = "NONE"

// Go to Phase 2 Continue Hub
$goto P3_Hub.Continue